# Generated parsers / compiler output
build/
target/
*.o
*.so
*.dylib

# Published stable compiler binary for downstream app teams.
# Pinned via scripts/publish-stable.sh; lives outside git so the
# in-flight refactor cycle on `target/release/hale` doesn't
# churn it underneath consumers.
/bin/

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Working notes (untracked by default; promote to notes/ when stable)
.scratch/

# Rust build artifacts
/target/
# Cargo.lock IS committed (binary workspace, reproducible builds).

# mdbook build output. Each doorway (and the archived book)
# builds under its own dir.
docs/**/book/

# Ferryman recognition output. Lands in <repo>/.ferryman/ wherever
# ferryman is pointed; the apps/operational-graph/fixture path
# is the in-repo smoke-test target.
.ferryman/

# experiments/token-efficiency lives on its own branch
# (experiments/token-efficiency). When that branch isn't checked
# out the dir still sits on disk; ignore its generated state so
# main's `git status` stays clean. Source files (briefs, tasks,
# harness, judges) are tracked on the branch, not here.
experiments/token-efficiency/.venv/
experiments/token-efficiency/workdirs/
experiments/token-efficiency/harness/runs.db
experiments/token-efficiency/.todo_storage*
**/__pycache__/

# Cross-session handoff / upstream working docs — not repo content
# (per CLAUDE.md: no planning/status/progress markdown in-tree).
HANDOFF-*.md
# GH #527 B2: the iris handoff record lives in-tree now.
!iris/handoffs/HANDOFF-*.md
UPSTREAM*.md

# Agent worktrees (transient; can hold root-owned build artifacts)
.claude/worktrees/

# Compiled Hale binaries have no rule here, on purpose. `hale build -o`
# puts a seed's binary under target/ (target/seeds/<name>/<name>), and
# `hale test`, `run` and `replay` build into a scratch directory they
# remove. A binary that turns up beside a source is a defect `git status`
# must show: the dna and face jobs fail on it, and
# crates/hale-cli/tests/seeds_build_out_of_tree.rs fails on a rule that
# would hide one.
# Secrets a local organism writes beside its compose file: not binaries.
/dna/**/nats.secrets.conf
/dna/**/postgres.secrets
